	Version 0.3.0.

	* src/newfile.h: Keep only the feature test macros, VERSION,
	BUG_URL, NEWFILE_BATCH and the attribute macros.  Move each
	declaration to the header of the file that defines it.
	* src/main.c (main): Parse the options, install the signal
	handlers, open the template and run the batches, then close
	standard output and standard error.  Fail when either cannot be
	closed.
	(reserve_std_fds): New function.
	(parse_options): Move to spec.c as spec_parse.
	(apply_size): Move to batch.c.
	(display_version): Move to options.c as options_version.
	(cleanup_handler): Move to pending.c.
	(setup_sighandlers): Move to pending.c as pending_install.
	(create_one, dirsync_error): Remove.
	* src/spec.c, src/spec.h: New files.
	(spec_parse): Return the index of the first operand.  Drop the
	umask fields.
	(spec_reset, spec_option, spec_misuse, spec_check, spec_values)
	(backup_control_known): New functions.  spec_values sets
	uid_changes when -o names a user other than the caller.
	* src/batch.c, src/batch.h: New files.
	(batch_run): New function.  Process operands in batches.  Build
	every file in a batch, flush them together, name them, flush them
	again with their directories, then report in operand order.  Stop
	the flush workers at the end.
	(build_one, open_built, finish_built): New functions.  Create an
	empty file with no owner and no exact mode in one open.  Build any
	other file unnamed, or under a temporary name created with mode
	0600.  Set its mode last, from the permission bits a new file gets
	in its directory and the requested set-user-ID, set-group-ID and
	sticky bits.  When -o gives the file to another user, give an
	unnamed file its temporary name before changing the owner.
	(fill_one, flush_batch, name_one, settle_batch, report_one)
	(op_fail, batch_size): New functions.
	(flush_ops, close_op, dir_unflushed): New functions.
	(settle_batch): Fail a file whose descriptor cannot be closed.
	(replace_one): New function.  Link the backup first.  Exchange the
	new file with the old where the filesystem can, otherwise flush
	the directory, then rename.  Block signals from the first exchange
	in a batch until drop_spares.
	(drop_spares): New function.  Remove the old files' temporary
	names once the directories are flushed.  Keep a name, with a
	warning, only where its own directory failed to flush.
	(settle_batch, drop_spares, replace_one, report_one): Fail the run
	when a temporary name cannot be removed from the file's directory.
	(apply_size): Move from main.c.  Take the size as 0 when nothing
	was copied into the file.
	* src/fileops.c: Remove.
	(pending_arm, pending_clear): Move to pending.c.
	(make_parents, dir_of, dir_prefix_len, ensure_directory): Move to
	paths.c.
	(make_backup): Move to backup.c as backup_make.
	(temp_open, pending_discard, pending_cleanup)
	(find_next_backup_number, dirsync_stage, dirsync_flush)
	(dirsync_dir, dirsync_release): Remove.
	* src/pending.c, src/pending.h: New files.
	(pending_arm, pending_clear): Move from fileops.c.  Track one name
	for each file in a batch and one for a backup.  pending_arm records
	the device and inode of the armed name.
	(pending_remove): New function.  Remove a name only while it holds
	the file it was armed with.  Report a name that cannot be removed,
	or that holds a different file and is kept, as an error, and
	return -1.
	(pending_retarget, pending_unlink): New functions.
	(pending_hold, pending_release): New functions.  Block every
	signal, then restore the mask.
	(cleanup_handler): Remove each armed name that still holds its
	file, then raise the signal again.  Exit with status 1 if it
	cannot be raised.
	(pending_install): Also catch SIGALRM, SIGUSR1, SIGUSR2, SIGILL,
	SIGTRAP, SIGABRT, SIGBUS, SIGFPE, SIGSEGV, SIGSYS, SIGVTALRM,
	SIGPROF, SIGPOLL, SIGPWR and SIGSTKFLT, each signal that not every
	architecture defines only where it is defined.
	* src/place.c, src/place.h: New files.
	(temp_make): New function.  Create under a free temporary name
	taken from getentropy.  Arm the name with signals blocked.
	(create_excl, temp_fill, make_open, make_fdlink, make_link): New
	functions.
	(place_create, place_temp, place_temp_link, place_temp_alias): New
	functions.
	(place_commit, place_over): New functions.  Name a temporary file
	by exclusive rename, then hard link, then over an empty 0600
	placeholder.  Report a placeholder that cannot be removed.
	(place_probe_mode, place_probe_reset): New functions.  Learn the
	mode a new file gets in a directory from an empty file, once per
	directory in a batch.
	(place_rename, place_exchange): New functions.  Update the armed
	names with signals blocked.
	* src/paths.c, src/paths.h: New files.
	(path_make_parents): Rename from make_parents.  Queue the
	directory holding each new directory for a flush.
	(path_dir, path_dir_len): Rename from dir_of and dir_prefix_len.
	* src/backup.c, src/backup.h: New files.
	(backup_make): Rename from make_backup.  Number from the highest
	existing backup, kept as decimal digits.  Skip a taken number
	instead of replacing it.  Move a simple backup in with rename.
	Probe .~1~ by name where the directory may not be read, and fail
	the backup on any other listing error.  Return 1 when the
	temporary name of a simple backup is left behind.
	(backup_cache_reset, backup_dir_get, backup_dir_list)
	(entries_keep_highest, backup_best, backup_find, backup_note)
	(backup_next): New functions.  List each directory's backups once
	per batch.  Keep a listing only once it succeeds.
	(backup_dir_free): New function.
	(backup_link): New function.  Arm the backup name with signals
	blocked.
	(first_backup_exists, digits_cmp, digits_inc, entry_cmp)
	(backup_split, backup_name, backup_numbered, backup_simple): New
	functions.
	* src/flush.c, src/flush.h: New files.
	(flush_fds): New function.  Flush several descriptors at once on
	worker threads, otherwise one after another.
	(flush_threaded, flush_take, flush_worker, flush_want, flush_grow)
	(flush_stop): New functions.  Start at most four workers per
	online CPU, with every signal blocked, and keep them for the run.
	Flush on the calling thread when no worker can start.  flush_stop
	returns the pool to its first state.
	(sync_one): Retry fsync interrupted with EINTR.
	(flush_dir, flush_set_init, flush_set_add, flush_set_run)
	(flush_set_failures): New functions.  Flush each directory that
	gained a name once, and count those that fail.  Flush a directory
	at once when it cannot be queued.
	(flush_set_failed, flush_set_forget, dir_failed): New functions.
	Record the directories that failed to flush in a batch.
	* src/io.c, src/io.h: New files.
	(io_write, io_pwrite): Move from template.c as write_buf and
